  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The framework's predictive accuracy depends heavily on the behavioral assumptions encoded as model parameters, which may not fully capture real-world human responses.",
      "what": "The researchers developed a simulation paradigm for ex-ante evaluation of urban traffic regulations by integrating a physical layer of mobility flows and emissions with a social layer of behavioral adaptation. The framework was tested using real-world data to compare a baseline scenario against multiple what-if scenarios representing broad traffic restriction schemes.",
      "why": "It provides a structured method to simulate both the direct physical impacts and the indirect behavioral responses of drivers before a policy is implemented, reducing the uncertainty of complex urban traffic interventions."
